  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Rwanda and the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) sign a peace agreement in Washington, D.C., United States, which calls for the \"disengagement, disarmament, and conditional integration\" of armed groups in the DRC, the return of refugees, and respect for territorial integrity. ((Yahoo! News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "The death toll from nationwide floods over the past 24 hours rises to 36 as at least 18 people are killed, ten others are missing and 58 people are rescued after flash floods triggered by pre-monsoon rains swept away dozens of tourists picnicking along the Swat River in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Pakistan. ((Deccan Herald)) ((CTV News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Nineteen people are killed and three others are injured when a minibus collides with a truck on a regional road in Ashmoun, Monufia, Egypt. ((CTV News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Seven city government personnel are killed while 18 others are injured after a government-owned mini dump truck returning from an environmental activity overturns in Silay, Negros Occidental, Philippines. ((Rappler))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Three people are killed when a Cessna 172 crashes in a residential area in Champhol, Centre-Val de Loire, France. ((Ouest-France)) ((Le Parisien))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "U.S. president Donald Trump announces the suspension of the trade talks with Canada, also announcing new tariffs on goods crossing the Canada–United States border. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "Serial killer and rapist Takahiro Shiraishi is executed for the 2017 murders and dismemberments of nine people in his apartment in Zama, Kanagawa Prefecture, Japan. ((CTV News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "The Supreme Court of the United States rules that all lower court orders on all nationwide injunctions exceeded their authority and should be limited, making it harder for district judges to have the power to entirely block presidential actions. This severely affects lower court cases involving illegal immigrant deportations and birthright citizenship. ((USA Today)) ((NPR))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Business and economy",
      "text": "The S&P 500 index closes at a record high of 6173.07 points, breaking the record set in February. ((NPR))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Sports",
      "text": "In ice hockey, the NHL entry draft is held at the Peacock Theater in Los Angeles, U.S., with the New York Islanders selecting Matthew Schaefer as the first overall pick. ((Sportsnet))"
    }
  ],
